[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2454994094","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98760#issuecomment-2454994094","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98760","id":2454994094,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6SVDyu","user":{"login":"DarioSamo","id":538504,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzODUwNA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/538504?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo","html_url":"https://github.com/DarioSamo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-04T15:20:00Z","updated_at":"2024-11-04T15:20:00Z","body":"I think `slice_trackers` should be turned into a pointer instead and allocate it on demand only if a shared texture is created. The HashMap currently occupies 48 bytes per texture and largely goes unused in the vast majority of cases. Then when the copy is made, the simple solution is to just set it to a nullptr. That way there'll be no cost from copying the contents as is and we get a reduced memory footprint overall, for the small extra cost of an indirection.\r\n\r\nI'm not a big fan of the proposed solution as it adds another function to maintain and keep track of when the copy is made.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/rep